WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.080
Game of Thrones fans have a rough understanding
of the Night King's origins and mission, there's

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.380
still so much to dig into as to why he did
what he did, whether he might rise again,

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.760
and just how he planned to take over the world
beyond Winterfell.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.360
The Night King's story begins with the story
of Westeros.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.100
Before the First Men came, the Children of
the Forest lived in harmony with the giants.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:27.659
Though they forged no metal, they developed
dragonglass — or as we know it, obsidian

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.880
— into useful tools and arrowheads, and
developed their unique magic.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:37.700
Unfortunately for them, the First Men invaded
the Children's land across a then-intact land

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:38.920
bridge from Essos.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.660
They brought bronze, masses of people, and
a thirst for conquest.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:48.240
Though the Children's magic was strong enough
to shatter the land bridge and separate the

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:53.190
two continents, it proved no match for the
sheer numbers and sturdy metal weaponry brought

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.180
by the First Men.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:59.270
In a last-ditch attempt to save their way
of life, the Children drove a dragonglass

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:04.470
dagger into a captured First Man, and used
their magic to transform him into an undead

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.460
being of ice.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:11.440
The Night King, first of his kind, had been
born into a world utterly unprepared for his

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.610
bottomless bloodlust.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:13.920
"It was you.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.040
You made the white walkers."

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.160
"We were at war."

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.680
Though the Children and the First Men did
ultimately end their hostilities, the Night

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.000
King and his undead disciples, known as White
Walkers, had become creatures of entirely

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:28.960
alien purpose.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.580
Game of Thrones never supplied any specifics
as to when the Night King turned his forces

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:39.940
against warm-blooded life, nor even how long,
precisely, their icy reign lasted.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.120
What is known is that the Night King and his
army of undead invaded northern Westeros,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.260
and an entire generation suffered and died
within the seemingly endless winter they brought.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.860
This became known as the Long Night, marked
by the failure of crops, massive casualties

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:01.100
by the sword, starvation, and sickness alike,
complete darkness, and the destruction of

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.240
organized settlements.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.060
It was, in the end, the closest the Night
King ever came to succeeding in his goal of

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.890
wiping out all life — and, as Bran Stark
later pointed out, all memory of life as well.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.650
Though the Night King and the White Walkers
never advanced beyond Westeros, their terror

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:18.780
became legendary.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.560
They were ultimately pushed back to the polar
wasteland through an enormous, conjoined effort

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:27.620
of magic, luck, and engineering referred to
as The War for the Dawn.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:34.220
Bran the Builder, an ancestor of House Stark,
erected a 700 foot-tall barrier known as the

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:38.140
Wall through a powerful blend of magic and
science so that the blue-eyed menace might

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:38.960
never return.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:44.200
Millennia passed, during which the Night King
and the Walkers became a long-ago threat,

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:49.120
a distant peril, and, finally, a story meant
to frighten children in the dead of night.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.260
Perhaps this was an intentional ploy on the
part of the Night King, whose immortality

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:56.820
meant he could wait a long time for his opportunity
to strike.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.470
The Long Night had given way to the dawn,
and the Night King bided his time for 8,000

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:03.460
years.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:08.840
At some point in the decades before the events
of Game of Thrones, the Night King demanded

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.920
a tribute from the Wildlings: male infants.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:18.140
As revealed in the season 4 episode "Oathkeeper:"
they were taken to the Lands of Always Winter,

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:22.560
laid upon icy altars, and turned into White
Walkers by the Night King himself.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.400
The process is apparently simple, yet notably
enigmatic.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:31.640
It's a notably different process than we see
when the Night King raises corpses as wights,

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:36.480
but we never learn how often it was done,
if every Walker had the power to do this,

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:41.180
nor how many human infants were turned over
the course of the 8,000-year retreat.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:46.459
Like so many things about the Night King and
his subjects, this horrifying element would

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.460
remain a mystery.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:53.120
Once he had gathered whatever number of corpses
and infant sacrifices that he thought would

00:03:53.129 --> 00:03:58.730
be enough to conquer Westeros the Night King
sent out his forces to harass, murder, and

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.400
generally terrorize the Wildlings.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:06.120
One especially horrible manifestation of this
campaign makes up the first scene of the show's

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.320
very first episode.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:13.379
Recall the Night's Watch deserter beheaded
by Ned Stark, the artfully arranged circle

00:04:13.379 --> 00:04:17.879
of corpse parts, and the dark shadow that
would be all the audience saw of the Walkers

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.460
until the season 2 finale.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.460
Westeros remained largely ignorant of the
threat — but some were not so lucky.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:29.710
The Walkers were making a statement, and the
Night King showed no interest in pulling back

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:30.900
as the rumors grew.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:35.640
In fact, it's likely that he was very purposefully
looking to sow that sort of fear.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:40.639
As the Wildlings grew more terrified, the
Night's Watch grew divided as to how to deal

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.140
with them.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:46.659
Dissent festered, culminating in Jon Snow's
murder and the mutiny against Lord Commander

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.160
Mormont.

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:52.480
The humans had been turned against themselves,
and all the Night King had to do was be there

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.440
to turn the corpses into his army.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:00.020
Years passed over the course of the first
five seasons of Game of Thrones while the

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:01.380
Night King gathered his strength.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.660
The Night's Watch came to understand the White
Walkers as a clear and present danger, finally

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:11.639
realizing that they were up against thousands
of corpses raised to fight against the living.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.980
It all came to a head in Season Five's "Hardhome."

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.580
Hardhome was the closest thing the Wildlings
ever had to a city.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.979
It's where Jon Snow, Tormund Giantsbane, and
a handful of Nights' Watchmen and like-minded

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:28.460
Wildlings traveled to urge its denizens to
join them in the fight against the Walkers.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.379
But their best-laid plans went belly-up when
the Walkers attacked just as the Wildling

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:36.580
boats set to sail to the Wall were beginning
to fill.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:43.060
An avalanche of wights overran the crude settlement,
slaying thousands in a savage surge of brutality.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:48.669
In the midst of the slaughter, Jon Snow discovered
Valyrian steel's resiliency against Walker

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:53.500
ice magic — and, immediately after, its
ability to shatter the beings themselves.

00:05:54.029 --> 00:05:58.099
Those fighting on the side of the living might
have learned something crucial about Valyrian

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.400
steel, but it came at a terrible cost.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:06.120
While Jon Snow and the Night's Watch were
battling the Walkers with sword and shield,

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:10.020
Bran Stark was on a crusade of his own, learning
to harness his psychic powers.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.180
Emboldened, he entered a vision, only to be
spotted by the Night King, who was able to

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:19.200
grab Bran's arm across miles of distance and
brand it with his mark.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:20.820
"But he can’t get in.”

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:22.560
“He can now."

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:28.040
Despite Hodor's tragic sacrifice and the Children's
magic, the Walkers were not stopped.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:33.920
Though the Three-Eyed Raven was able to pass
on his powers to Bran, he still fell to the

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:39.040
Night King's spear, along with many of what
might have been the only Children of the Forest

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:39.540
left.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:45.550
In stripping Bran of his most important allies,
protectors, and teachers, he managed to further

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.700
that goal considerably.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:52.960
As the Night King neared the Wall, Jon Snow
proposed something drastic: gathering a party

00:06:52.969 --> 00:06:57.659
of warriors to capture a wight that would
prove the truth of the threat to Queen Cersei

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.160
and her skeptical court.

00:06:59.749 --> 00:07:04.539
Though the grizzled band was, in fact, able
to present the queen with a real-deal blue-eyed

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.720
corpse, it came at tremendous cost.

00:07:07.569 --> 00:07:12.860
The Walkers and their army killed much of
the group, including Viserion, one of Daenerys

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.780
Targeryan's trio of dragons.

00:07:14.949 --> 00:07:19.740
The fact that Cersei didn't join forces with
Daenerys and Jon in the war against the Walkers

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:20.740
is cruel enough.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:25.980
But even worse, The Night King was able to
raise Viserion as an undead dragon, complete

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:29.120
with the ability to breathe massively destructive
blue fire.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:33.580
Jon Snow might have accomplished what he set
out to do in the most literal sense, but on

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:38.080
a much more important scale, this was yet
another victory for the Night King.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:42.580
The army of death had only grown in its size
and sinister capabilities.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.880
"The Night King is coming."

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.420
"The dead are already here."

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:54.680
It wasn't long before the Night King decided
to put his brand new steed to the test.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:08:01.340
Leading untold thousands of resurrected corpses,
a host of mounted White Walkers, and a fearsome

00:08:01.349 --> 00:08:06.020
number of undead beasts, the Night King descended
upon the castle of Eastwatch-by-the-Sea with

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:07.040
frozen fury.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:13.340
One fiery assault from Viserion was all it
took to pierce the wall — thousands of tons

00:08:13.349 --> 00:08:18.809
of enchanted ice, rock, and masonry fell beneath
the eerie blue flame, leaving a clear road

00:08:18.809 --> 00:08:20.160
through to Westeros.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:25.620
It was this shocking image that closed out
the seventh season finale of Game of Thrones:

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:29.160
the last, best defense of the living, torn
asunder at last.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:34.500
The Wall, which had stood for 8,000 years,
had fallen before the Night King and his seemingly

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:35.740
unstoppable army.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:40.930
All he had left to do was massacre his prey,
starting with Winterfell and all the living

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.419
souls who dwelt within.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.620
The Night King advanced upon the North quickly.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.420
His first stop was the Last Hearth, the home
of House Umber.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:53.780
Though battered by the war and tasked with
maintaining a remote position between the

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:59.470
unknown wastes and the comforts of Winterfell,
Umber was a proud house with a long and glorious

00:08:59.470 --> 00:08:59.980
history.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:05.260
In the aftermath of the Battle of the Bastards,
the house was headed by Lord Ned Umber, a

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:09.220
ten-year-old looking to regain the honor lost
when his family backed the Boltons.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:13.360
"Will you stand beside me, Ned and Alys, now
and always?"

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:18.080
Unfortunately, the Night King made that "always"
quite a bit shorter than it should have been.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:22.880
The Last Hearth was the Walkers' first stop
on the way to Winterfell, and after slaughtering

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.640
Ned Umber and his household, they left a grim
warning behind in the form of their characteristic

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.040
spiral of body parts.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:34.640
Though Ned was prevented from causing more
carnage as a wight courtesy of a flaming sword,

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:38.360
killing Umber stands as one of the saddest
crimes the Night King perpetrated.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:43.500
With the Wall breached, the armies massed,
a dragon risen from the grave and the living

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:48.110
forces of Westeros getting their hands on
every ounce of dragonglass that they could,

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:49.980
there was no more time for preparation.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.320
Instead, it was war.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:57.410
The Night King descended upon Winterfell like
a tempest, swallowing the fires of Dothraki

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:02.120
warriors, trenches of flame and valiant charges
alike within his icy darkness.

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:06.860
Beyond the mayhem and death that he brought
with him, the Night King had a mission: to

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:11.180
find Bran Stark, the new Three-Eyed Raven,
and kill him.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.700
Bran knew this, and allowed himself to be
used as bait.

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:20.030
The stakes were high — Theon Greyjoy died
in his efforts to protect Bran, the dead in

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:24.460
the crypts and on the battlefields of Winterfell
were raised by the Night King's powers, and

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:28.400
Jon Snow resorted to facing Viserion with
nothing but a sword.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:34.300
Then, out of nowhere, came Arya Stark, honed
into one of the finest warriors alive.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:40.440
With one swift stab the Night King was slain,
along with all the creatures he'd created.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.900
The army of the dead was gone.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.080
An eternity of winter had been avoided.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:50.180
And the White Walkers, with the death of their
leader and progenitor, instantly became extinct.

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.780
Thus ended the war audiences had been teased
with for years.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:11:00.560
With Arya's devastatingly precise stab, she
vanquished the White Walkers completely.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:04.920
The Night King's reign of terror lives on,
however, in the hearts of Game of Thrones'

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:06.200
principal characters.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:11.520
Jon Snow, free at last to live beyond titles
and great houses, cannot ever rid himself

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.840
of the evil he stared down, and returns to
the Night's Watch.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:19.880
Bran, elevated to king, is also tasked with
remembering what brought the Walkers about

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:20.820
in the first place.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:26.080
Arya, off on adventures beyond the borders
of Westeros, will doubtlessly be followed

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:29.740
everywhere she goes by the fact of her great,
world-saving deed.

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:35.220
These, and many other characters, now live
in a Westeros that's as much defined by the

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.980
Night King's absence as it was by his presence.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:43.150
The Night King might be dead, but his memory
will linger on for years to come — if only

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:44.660
as a terrifying fairytale.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:47.240
